{
  "title": "Pur avendo studiato, non {pr:superò} l'esame",
  "translation": "Despite having studied, he didn't pass the exam",
  "topics": "Infinitive, gerund and participle in shortened clauses, keeping track of the subject",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "Who is doing the action?"
      },
      "A gerund or an infinitive has no subject of its own, so it takes that of the main verb. This rule prevents a very common mistake.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Wrong",
            "Right"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Entrando in casa, il telefono squillò.",
              "Mentre {im:entravo} in casa, il telefono squillò."
            ],
            [
              "Essendo in ritardo, il capo si {pp:è arrabbiato} con me.",
              "Poiché {im:ero} in ritardo, il capo si {pp:è arrabbiato} con me."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "The first wrong sentence says that the telephone was entering the house.",
      {
        "h": "The participle can have its own subject"
      },
      "Unlike the gerund, the absolute participle can have a subject that differs from the main verb. It comes after the participle: *Partito il treno, {pr:tornammo} a casa*. A gerund can do this only in formal style: *Essendo il treno partito, {pr:tornammo} a casa*.",
      {
        "h": "One idea, several shortened forms"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Meaning",
            "Form",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Time",
              "nel + infinitive",
              "Nel vederla, {pr:sorrise}."
            ],
            [
              "Time",
              "absolute participle",
              "Finita la cena, {pr:uscimmo}."
            ],
            [
              "Cause",
              "gerund",
              "Non avendo soldi, {pr:rinunciò}."
            ],
            [
              "Cause",
              "per + past infinitive",
              "{pr:Fu licenziato} per aver mentito."
            ],
            [
              "Condition",
              "a + infinitive",
              "A pensarci bene, {ip:hai} ragione."
            ],
            [
              "Condition",
              "gerund",
              "Partendo ora, {cop:arriveresti} in tempo."
            ],
            [
              "Concession",
              "pur + gerund",
              "Pur avendo studiato, non {pr:superò} l'esame."
            ],
            [
              "Result",
              "da + infinitive",
              "{ip:È} così stanco da non reggersi in piedi."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "The tense of the shortened form"
      },
      "The simple form shows that the action happens at the same time. The compound form shows that it comes first.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Same time",
            "Before"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Studiando, ascolto musica.",
              "Avendo studiato, {pp:ho superato} l'esame."
            ],
            [
              "{ip:Credo} di capire.",
              "{ip:Credo} di aver capito."
            ],
            [
              "Prima di partire",
              "Dopo essere partito"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "With a past infinitive, *essere* verbs keep their agreement with the subject: *Dopo essere arrivat**a**, Anna {pr:telefonò}.*"
    ]
  },
